---

<DocsLayout
  title="Source Map"
  subtitle="A practical map for finding the real implementation behind CLI commands, API routes, TUI views, mobile flows, providers, plugins, and storage."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="overview" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      The main runtime lives in <code>packages/nikcli/src</code>. The repo is a Bun monorepo, so
      related packages also matter: <code>packages/sdk/js</code> for generated client types,
      <code>packages/plugin</code> for plugin contracts, <code>packages/mobile</code> for the Expo
      app, <code>packages/web</code> for this docs site, <code>packages/llm</code> for route-based
      LLM providers, and <code>packages/remote</code> for remote execution support.
    </p>
    <p>
      This map is meant for tracing behavior from a symptom to the source. Start at the command or
      route entry, then follow service imports into the domain module.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="top-level-entry" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Top-level entry</h2>
    <p>
      <code>packages/nikcli/src/index.ts</code> registers every CLI command with yargs, initializes
      global directories, initializes logging, sets <code>AGENT=1</code> and <code>NIKCLI=1</code>,
      and catches fatal errors for user-facing formatting.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash">
bun run --cwd packages/nikcli --conditions=browser src/index.ts --help
bun run --cwd packages/nikcli --conditions=browser src/index.ts serve --help
bun run --cwd packages/nikcli --conditions=browser src/index.ts mcp --help
    </DocCode>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Need</th><th>Start here</th><th>Then inspect</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Command registration</td><td><code>src/index.ts</code></td><td><code>src/cli/cmd/*.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Global paths</td><td><code>src/global/index.ts</code></td><td><code>NIKCLI_DATA_DIR</code>, XDG/AppData rules.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Logging</td><td><code>src/util/log.ts</code></td><td><code>--print-logs</code>, <code>--log-level</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Error formatting</td><td><code>src/cli/error.ts</code></td><td>Command-specific thrown errors.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="runtime-domains" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Runtime domains</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-8">
      <DocCard title="CLI and TUI" eyebrow="Entry">
        <p><code>src/cli/cmd</code> contains commands. <code>src/cli/cmd/tui</code> contains the OpenTUI/Solid renderer, worker RPC, routes, dialogs, plugins, and contexts.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Server" eyebrow="HTTP">
        <p><code>src/server/server.ts</code> owns middleware and route mounting. <code>src/server/routes</code> owns classic routes. <code>src/server/httpapi</code> owns typed route groups.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Sessions" eyebrow="Agent">
        <p><code>src/session</code> owns session lifecycle, prompt execution, LLM normalization, messages, status, revert, compaction, todo, and stats.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Extensions" eyebrow="Tools">
        <p><code>src/plugin</code>, <code>src/mcp</code>, <code>src/connectors</code>, <code>src/skill</code>, and <code>src/tool</code> expose extra capabilities to agents.</p>
      </DocCard>
    </div>
  </section>

