  <section id="trace-feature" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>How to trace a feature</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Find the entry: command in <code>src/index.ts</code>, route in <code>server.ts</code>, or UI route in <code>tui/context/route.tsx</code>.</li>
      <li>Read the domain service imported by that entry. Route files usually call services from <code>session</code>, <code>provider</code>, <code>config</code>, <code>mcp</code>, <code>connectors</code>, or <code>workspace</code>.</li>
      <li>Check config and flags. Many features are enabled by config fields plus environment flags from <code>flag/flag.ts</code>.</li>
      <li>Check storage. Durable behavior usually writes through <code>Storage.Service</code> or a SQLite helper.</li>
      <li>For client behavior, trace generated SDK types in <code>packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen</code> and UI code in <code>packages/mobile</code> or TUI route files.</li>
    </ol>
    <DocCode language="bash">
rg -n "route-or-command-name" packages/nikcli/src
rg -n "operationId|HttpApiEndpoint|get\\(|post\\(" packages/nikcli/src/server
rg -n "Config\\.Service|Provider\\.Service|Session\\.Service" packages/nikcli/src
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="directory-table" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
